.TH "RECORD\-TRUNCATE\-DATABASE\.PY" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-truncate\-database\.py\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-truncate\-database\.py\fR \fB\-\-force\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-truncate\-database\.py\fR removes all rows from every table in the RECORD provenance database without dropping the schema\. It is a destructive maintenance utility and requires explicit confirmation via \fB\-\-force\fR before any write is performed\.
.P
The script is only meaningful for relational backends\. If \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBgremlin\fR, the script exits with an advisory message directing the user to \fBdelete\-database\.py\fR instead, as truncation is not a applicable concept for a graph database\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Required\. Instructs the script to proceed with truncation\. Without this flag the script prints a refusal message to standard error and exits with status 1\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success\.
.P
Returns 1 if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fB\-\-force\fR is not supplied; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBgremlin\fR (advisory exit, no truncation attempted)\.
.IP "" 0
.P
Returns non\-zero if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
the \fBrecord\fR library cannot be imported from \fBlib/\fR; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
a database error occurs during \fBempty_tables\fR, \fBconnect_db\fR, or \fBdisconnect_db\fR\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
The script inherits all database connection environment variables from the \fBrecord\fR library\. Refer to \fBrecord\.py\fR for the full list, including:
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Selects the database backend\. One of \fBsqlite3\fR, \fBpostgres\fR, or \fBgremlin\fR\. If set to \fBgremlin\fR, truncation is skipped and an advisory message is printed\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBFILE\fR
Path to the SQLite database file\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBsqlite3\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBUSER\fR
PostgreSQL username\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBNAME\fR
PostgreSQL database name\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_HOST\fR
PostgreSQL hostname\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PORT\fR
PostgreSQL port number\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PASSWORD\fR
PostgreSQL password\. Required when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR
When set, enables verbose diagnostic output to standard error\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
This script produces no output on success\. Diagnostic messages are written to standard error when debug mode is active or when truncation is refused\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Truncate all tables in the database:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-truncate\-database\.py \-\-force
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Attempt truncation without confirmation (will be refused):
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-truncate\-database\.py
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib/record\.py\fR
The RECORD provenance library\. Must be importable as \fBrecord\fR; the script appends \fBlib\fR to \fBsys\.path\fR before importing, so \fBrecord\.py\fR must be present in a \fBlib/\fR subdirectory relative to the working directory\.
