.SH "BUGS"
Debug output is unconditionally enabled by \fBrecord\.debug = True\fR at module level in \fBrecord\.py\fR and cannot be suppressed via the \fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR environment variable\.
.P
When \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBgremlin\fR the script writes the advisory message to standard error but exits with status 0 rather than a non\-zero status, making it indistinguishable from a successful truncation in automated pipelines\.
